Subject: [PATCH 090/119] docs: the export, the two round trips, and what a
 difference means

docs/SceneReferredExport.md: the two taps and why they are two different artefacts rather than two
settings of one, the commands, what a sequence does to t_FixedStep and the jitter phase, the two
encodings and which one Resolve reads without being told anything, the metadata list with the three
attributes that are load-bearing rather than decorative, and both acceptance procedures - the
automatable one against OCIO and the manual one against Resolve, including the Resolve project
settings that silently produce a wrong answer (ACES 1.x, Video data levels).

The most useful part is the last table: the SHAPE of a difference names its cause. A uniform offset
is data levels or exposure; error growing with luminance is a wrong input transform or a doubled
gamma; error only in saturated colour is the ACEScct shaper's negative clamp; error only where the
vignette is dark means the vignette is inside the tap on one side and not the other.

ConsoleReference gains the three commands and the five cvars. The spec's S6 section records the
status and the five deviations earned here - the tap being converted back to linear rather than
left in ACEScct, AP0 rather than AP1 as the default encoding, tinyexr living in Code/Libs, two taps
instead of one, and rec/lensName published empty until lens presets exist - plus the note that S4's
own acceptance test finally has an instrument.

