+### rec_CaptureEXR / rec_CaptureEXRStop / rec_CaptureEXRFrame
+
+```
+rec_CaptureEXR [folder] [prefix]
+rec_CaptureEXRStop
+rec_CaptureEXRFrame [folder] [prefix]
+```
+
+Write the scene-referred frame to OpenEXR - half float, ACES primaries, with the camera's own
+settings in the header. `rec_CaptureEXR` starts a sequence and runs until `rec_CaptureEXRStop`;
+`rec_CaptureEXRFrame` writes exactly one and disarms.
+
+Relative folders land under the user folder, absolute paths are taken as given, and the folder is
+created if it does not exist (default `CaptureEXR`). Files are `<prefix>.%06d.exr` (default prefix
+`frame`) - dot-separated, which is what Nuke and Resolve auto-detect as a sequence. The frame
+counter belongs to the capture and starts at zero on every arm; it is **not** `capture_frames`,
+which `ManualFrameStep` and CryMovie also write, and none of the stock capture path is touched.
+
+Nothing is written unless the camera's **Scene Referred** path is running - off it there is no
+pre-ODT buffer to tap.
+
+A **sequence** sets `t_FixedStep` (see `r_SceneReferredExportFixedStep`) and freezes the lens
+model's jitter phase (`r_DepthOfFieldLensModelJitter 2`) for its duration, restoring both on stop.
+A single frame leaves them alone. If the readback or the disk falls behind, the capture stops and
+says so rather than dropping a frame.
+
+What is written is decided by the four `r_SceneReferredExport*` cvars below, all latched at the
+moment the capture starts. The full procedure, the metadata list and the Resolve/OCIO round trip
+are in [SceneReferredExport.md](SceneReferredExport.md).
+
